## Install

1. Drop the `Scripts/` folder into your project's `Assets/`.
{% if s.backend == "UIToolkit" %}
2. Drop the `UI/` folder (UXML + USS) into `Assets/UI/`. Make sure the UI Toolkit
   package is enabled (built in for Unity 6).
3. Add a `UIDocument` component to a Canvas-less GameObject and assign `{{ s.name }}.uxml`.
4. Add the `{{ s.name }}` component to the same GameObject and wire its `document` field.
{% else %}
2. Add a `Canvas` to your scene if you don't already have one. Set Render Mode to
   `Screen Space - Overlay`.
3. Add the `{{ s.name }}` component to a child GameObject under the Canvas and wire
   the SerializeField references in the inspector.
{% endif %}
{% if s.binding == "events" %}
4. Call the public API (`SetHealth`, `SetAmmo`, `Show`, `Hide`, …) from your game code.
{% else %}
4. The HUD polls singletons each frame — adapt the `Update()` body to find your sources.
{% endif %}
